+
+# Spike: Session Handover
+
+## Problem
+
+Handover docs are hand-written at end of session, go stale within the same
+session, and require manual cross-referencing of git log / todos / planning
+status / open GitHub issues. Agents starting a new session have to reconstruct
+state from multiple scattered sources.
+
+## Goal
+
+A `scripts/handover.sh` that auto-generates `tmp/session-handover-$(date +%Y-%m-%d).md`
+from live sources, structured for agent pickup with zero manual work.
+
+## Inputs to aggregate
+
+| Source | What to pull |
+|--------|-------------|
+| `git log main --since="24 hours ago"` | what shipped (commit messages) |
+| `bun run planning:status` | epic status table |
+| `.pi/todos/` | open todos grouped by tag |
+| `gh issue list --state open` | open GitHub issues (if gh CLI available) |
+| `git branch -a` | any live worktrees / feature branches |
+| `git status` | uncommitted work |
+
+## Output format
+
+```
+# Session Handover — YYYY-MM-DD
+
+## Branch State          (git status + branches)
+## What Shipped Today    (git log --since 24h, formatted)
+## Epic Status           (planning:status output)
+## Open Todos            (grouped: bugs / planning / creative)
+## Open GitHub Issues    (gh issue list)
+## Recommended Next Steps (derived from in-progress epics + open todos)
+```
+
+## Integration points
+
+- `planning-update` skill closeout ceremony: call `bash scripts/handover.sh` as final step
+- AGENTS.md: document as "end of session" action
+- `bun run handover` alias in package.json
+
+## Success criteria
+
+- `bash scripts/handover.sh` runs in < 5s without the app running
+- Output is parseable by a fresh agent session without reading anything else
+- No manual edits needed for > 80% of handover content
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Real-time updates during session
+- Pushing handover to GitHub as a PR description
+- Summarising with LLM (keep it deterministic)
+
+## Estimated effort
+
+Half a day. Pure bash + existing CLI tools.
